<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal's TAP to lease 22 Airbus planes.</title>
<headline>Portugal's TAP to lease 22 Airbus planes.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portugal's TAP-Air Portugal will lease 22 Airbus Industrie medium-haul planes, a spokesman for Planning Minister Joao Cravinho said.</p>
<p>He said the contract was worth 70 billion escudos.</p>
<p>The European air consortium Airbus and Boeing, which provides most of TAP's current fleet, both bid for the contract.  </p>
<p>&quot;(Planning) Minister Joao Cravinho decided to opt for Airbus rather than Boeing this morning on the advice of TAP management,&quot; the spokesman said.</p>
<p>Airbus had been widely tipped to land the deal.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +(351-1) 3538254</p>
